<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Ireland sets June 6 for general election poll.</title>
<headline>Ireland sets June 6 for general election poll.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish prime minister John Bruton told parliament on Thursday that he plans to dissolve the Irish parliament.</p>
<p>Bruton said he intended to go to Irish president Mary Robinson to request permission to dissolve Ireland's 27th parliament. Officials said the election would be held on June 6 and that parliament would reconvene on June 26.</p>
</text>
